- TRAVEL: Do NOT estimate travel time or distance — the TimeKeeper step handles that. Focus on
  whether the travel action requires any mechanical checks (Survival for navigation, Fortitude
  for forced march, etc.).
- ENVIRONMENTAL HAZARDS: account for swim checks (DC varies by water conditions), climb checks
  (DC by surface), balance checks on narrow/slippery surfaces, and weather effects (visibility,
  movement penalties in heavy rain/snow).
- MOVEMENT IN DIFFICULT TERRAIN: each square of difficult terrain costs 2 squares of movement.
  Running and charging are not possible in difficult terrain unless the character has special
  abilities.
